&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the strategy and roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product and Design to set a multi-quarter roadmap for declarative deployment: agentic development, governed deployments and deployment history, enterprise CI/CD, and new resource coverage. Make the trade-offs explicit when the demand is larger than the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar on execution and operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Run a predictable delivery process for a fast-moving, open-source product with frequent releases. Own reliability, on-call health, incident response and the quality bar for a tool customers depend on to ship to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treat backward compatibility as a product feature:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead engine and configuration migrations without forcing customers through a flag day, and communicate change clearly to customers, the community and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead across the platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive alignment with the many platform teams whose resources and services the framework deploys, and with our sibling teams in Developer Ecosystem (SDKs, CLI, IaC provider, IDE). Make the whole toolchain feel like one product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing software engineering teams, and 8+ years of software engineering experience overall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and shipping developer tools or platforms used by many external developers or internal teams, such as infrastructure-as-code, deployment or CI/CD systems, CLIs, SDKs, or internal developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of declarative systems and deployment workflows: plan/apply, state management, drift and reconciliation, environment promotion, GitOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical depth to engage on architecture and trade-offs with senior and staff engineers, and to hold a high-quality bar for public, versioned interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams through ambiguity, with competing priorities from customers, partners and platform dependencies, and making clear calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and a customer-first mindset. You enjoy talking to developers, reading their issues, and turning feedback into roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including with executives, partner teams and an external developer community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stand-out experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or led teams on infrastructure-as-code or deployment platforms, e.g. Terraform, Pulumi, AWS CDK / CloudFormation, Kubernetes controllers, Argo CD / Flux / Helm, or Vercel / Netlify-style deploy platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed an open-source developer tool with an active community and a frequent release cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped developer workflows for AI coding agents (CLI-first tooling, agent skills, MCP), or AI-assisted authoring.&lt;/li&gt;
